# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs explicit paths, so this file is not a security boundary on its own —
# its job is to keep the context small (node_modules alone is ~170 MB) and to keep the
# build cache from being invalidated by files that have nothing to do with the image.
#
# The three lines that matter most are .env, *.sqlite and .git: a secret, a household's entire
# financial history, and every version of both.

# --- installed and generated ------------------------------------------------
node_modules
app/node_modules
app/dist
gen
@cds-models
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variant, because `.env.production` and `.env.local.bak` are the same mistake.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- data -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live ledger and its WAL/shm sidecars. The image ships an empty database that the
# entrypoint creates on the volume; it must never ship a populated one.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.sqlite-journal
backups
db.sqlite
db.sqlite-wal
db.sqlite-shm

# --- machine learning -------------------------------------------------------
# `ml/model/weights.json` is deliberately NOT ignored — the Dockerfile copies it and the
# classifier is dead without it. Everything else in ml/ is a laptop concern: the venv
# (hundreds of MB), the generated training CSVs, the pickled sklearn model (~7 MB, only
# `ml/export_ts.py` reads it) and the parity fixture (a test input).
ml/.venv
ml/__pycache__
ml/data
ml/aicore
ml/model/*.pkl
ml/model/parity_fixture.json
**/__pycache__

# --- version control and CI -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- tests and their output -------------------------------------------------
test
vitest.config.mts
app/e2e
app/playwright.config.ts
playwright-report
test-results

# --- editor, OS, docs -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode
.idea
docs
*.md
!README.md
